        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Mappings are already possible, and are, by design, the user-level way of defining normal-mode cmds. Similar to how lowercase cmdline-commands cannot be defined by plugins, that hard separation is an important invariant. And there is no strong reason to upend it.\n\nAnyway, I'm going to close this because it seems to be mixing up multiple concepts. E.g., a better interface for defining textobjects is tracked in:\n\n- https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/8544",
